$ signet sandbox replay --help
-- stdout --
Re-run a repro bundle (signet sandbox export) with no network access: the
host is opened with fetching denied, loaded with the bundle's entries, network
config and overrides, and every call runs on the deployed and the built WASM
from the same state, as signet dev ran it. Each side's outcome and return value
must match the bundle's expected results; any mismatch exits 10.

--wasm replaces the built WASM, to try a fix against someone's repro (the
expected results are then the old build's, so a changed call is a mismatch).
A bundle recorded on a simulator lane this build does not have exits 11, and
an edited bundle (its bundleHash no longer matches) exits 2.

--stream writes every call's full A and B results as NDJSON: the same bundle
gives the same bytes on every platform, which CI checks.

Usage:
  signet sandbox replay <bundle.json> [flags]

Examples:
  signet sandbox replay repro.json
  signet sandbox replay repro.json --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/registry.wasm

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for replay
      --stream string   write every call's full A and B results here, as NDJSON
      --wasm string     a WASM to run as the build instead of the bundle's

Global Flags:
      --context string              deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --drift string                when an entry fetched for the fork changed on-chain after the fork ledger: warn, fail (exit 6), or refork (pin the latest ledger and run once more) (default "warn")
      --insecure                    allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                        write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string              Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --network-passphrase string   passphrase of a custom --network (checked against the RPC's getNetwork)
      --rpc-url string              Stellar RPC to fork from (overrides the context's rpc-url; testnet defaults to https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org)
      --sign-with-key string        identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string               identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string                  Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)
-- stderr --
(empty)
-- exit 0 --
